  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1042 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nA few showers may linger around Sunday evening and early overnight, \nbut additional amounts will remain light. Dry weather is then \nexpected through mid week as heights increase and the sfc high \nexpands back into the region. This will also result in warming \ntemperatures. By Tuesday and Wednesday, highs are likely to increase \nback into the 60s. Locations across far NE OK and NW AR may \nexperience near freezing temperatures Sunday night and Monday \nnight, where cloud cover is thinner or clears. Lows in the 40s or \ngreater are likely thereafter.\n\nA shortwave will rapidly move northeast across the central plains\nlate Wednesday and potentially brush the northwestern edge of CWA\nwith a weak cold front. At this time, impacts appear negligible \nwith this system. Deterministic and ensemble guidance then \nindicate a stronger trough will swing through the plains next \nweekend and provide higher rain chances as well as potential for a\nsignificant cool down. However, exact details and impacts vary at\nthis range.",
